- `ui-tests`: `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests`

**How to implement.** The Materials window imports a glass catalogue the user picks, and one dropped on it, through the import dialog (001 §D; 001 §O; .spec-md §10.1 discoverability: the import dialog opens on a dropped entry file, and the window offers the verb; §10.3 identify → confirm; §10.4: the dialog's completion message re-renders the window; 001 §P: the button and the test send the same message). A dropped `.agf` file already decides through `DropMaterialEntryFiles` (step 110) and `decideDroppedFiles` (step 463); this step adds the verb and its message. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S13.2. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialsWindowView.fs`: (a) the public `pickGlassCatalogueFile (owner : Window) (onPicked : FileName -> unit) : unit` is the open dialog, an IO edge in `pickEntryExportFile`'s shape (step 119): `owner.StorageProvider.OpenFilePickerAsync` with `Title = "Import glass catalogue"`, `AllowMultiple = false` and one `FilePickerFileType` `Zemax glass catalogue` whose pattern is `*.agf`; a confirmed file's `Path.LocalPath` is passed as a `FileName`, posted on the UI thread, and a host without a provider changes nothing. (b) `MaterialsWindowMsg` gains `ImportGlassCatalogue of FileName`, documented in one line. (c) `updateMaterialsWindow`: `ImportGlassCatalogue file` answers what `DropMaterialEntryFiles [ file ]` answers (step 110), both arms calling one private helper over the file list: `Ok decisions` opens the import dialog over them (`context.openImportDialog`) and clears the import status and error; `Error e` sets `importError`. (d) The verbs row (`MaterialsWindowView.fs:verbsRow`), in Browse mode, after step 452's `Online sources…`: `verbButtonOn ConstructorUiId.materialsImportGlassCatalogueButton (ControlCaption "Import glass catalogue…")`, resolving the owner window from the press as `materialsExportButton` does (step 119), calls `pickGlassCatalogueFile owner (fun file -> dispatch (ImportGlassCatalogue file))`. Select mode never shows it. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialsWindow.fs`: `member _.ImportGlassCatalogue (file : FileName) : unit` dispatches `ImportGlassCatalogue file`, the semantic seam the verb and the tests share, as `DropEntryFiles` is the drop's (step 110); the class doc names it in no more words. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`, the Materials window group (`UiIds.fs:525`): `materialsImportGlassCatalogueButton` (`"MaterialsImportGlassCatalogueButton"`) under a one-line comment citing spec 0050 S13.2. (4) Tests, in `MaterialsWindowTests`, each AGF file written by the fact into a fresh GUID folder under `Path.Combine(AppContext.BaseDirectory, "MaterialsWindowTests")`: a test-local two-glass text, `LAB-A` (formula 2) and `LAB-B` (formula 1), ASCII. `the glass-catalogue UiId of the Materials window is the stable intent-named id`: the id's text. `ImportGlassCatalogue decides the catalogue's glasses and opens the import dialog, applying nothing`: over `stubContext` (steps 110, 119, 452) with its recording `openImportDialog`, `ImportGlassCatalogue` of the file records one dialog holding two `EntryIdNotHeld` rows named `LAB-A` and `LAB-B` under `FileImportProvenance`, the context's import seam holding neither; `ImportGlassCatalogue` of a missing file sets `importError` to `DroppedFileRefusedErr` and records no dialog. `Import glass catalogue… is offered in Browse mode only`: the Browse view shows `materialsImportGlassCatalogueButton` and a Select-mode view does not. With trait `ui-smoke`: `acceptance: a glass catalogue imported in the Materials window adds its glasses to the app library`: over `AppContext.create (TestAppScope.fileLocations (FolderName "MaterialsWindowTests")) WorkbenchSettings.defaults` (step 88), a `MaterialsWindow` built as the launcher builds it is shown headless; `window.ImportGlassCatalogue` of the file opens exactly one `ImportDialogWindow`, observed through `Window.WindowOpenedEvent` as `LauncherTests.clickAndObserve` observes; pressing its `importApplyButton` closes it, `ctx.materials.tryGetMaterial` resolves both glasses in the Glass category, and `materialsImportStatusText` shows the summary.

**Acceptance.** After the verb is wired, the Materials window MUST offer `Import glass catalogue…` in Browse mode, and `ImportGlassCatalogue` MUST open the import dialog over the catalogue's glasses as a drop of the file does; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `acceptance: a glass catalogue imported in the Materials window adds its glasses to the app library`, the count rising by 1; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected class, including `the glass-catalogue UiId of the Materials window is the stable intent-named id`, `ImportGlassCatalogue decides the catalogue's glasses and opens the import dialog, applying nothing` and `Import glass catalogue… is offered in Browse mode only`, the count rising by 3; and build, elevation and the twenty-one s44 invariants MUST pass.
